          },
          "mechanism": "Housing transitions are not direct causes of antihistamine use or HIV diagnosis age.",
          "justification": "While housing stability might proxy for socioeconomic status or healthcare access, these are already captured by income, insurance, and other covariates, and recent moves do not causally influence historical antihistamine use patterns or the timing of past HIV diagnosis.",
